// "Choose" — the clear fighter choice (Eddie, 2026-11-16,
// refined 09:26 PT): "There needs to be a clear CHOOSE button on
// the Navidex page."
//
// Streamlined (Eddie, 2026-11-16 ~13:17 PT): "the choosing
// option is too redundant" — and the model, stated exactly: "You
// should choose your fighter in Navidex, it will then fight or
// stroll for you, then when a battle comes you should have a
// choice to swap fighters." So choosing happens in ONE place:
// the Navidex, for the staged fighter. Grid cards no longer carry
// a Choose BUTTON (tapping a card stages the fighter; the card's
// ✓ CHOSEN badge/ring still shows state), Battle offers only a
// Swap sheet (QuickSwapNavitar), never a re-pick, and there is no
// "Go to Battle" button here — the bottom tab bar's Battle tab is
// always one tap away.
//
// THE CHECK (Eddie, 2026-11-16 ~13:46 PT): "there should be a
// check on the screen on the card of the Nav — that's where you
// pick your avatar right there. Click the check and it takes over
// the role of being with you." So every unlocked navitar CARD —
// the Stage's staged-fighter card and the Navidex grid cards —
// carries a ✓ check control (ChooseCheckButton below): tap it and
// that navitar is chosen, right there, no staging round-trip.
// The check and the Stage's big "✔ Choose for Battle" button are
// the same action wearing two sizes: both go through
// useChooseNavitar, which writes the SINGLE existing source of
// truth — there is exactly one selection state underneath.
//
// Behaviour, exactly:
// - Tap Choose (either control) → that navitar becomes the
//   player's ACTIVE navitar, in place, with instant confirmation.
//   NO navigation, NO battle starts. Choosing alone never starts
//   anything — battle law still requires (2) approve opponent and
//   (3) press START BATTLE on /battle.
// - Once chosen, the controls flip to their highlighted state —
//   the button reads "✓ Chosen — Your Battle Navitar", the check
//   fills gold.
// - Only one chosen at a time: setActiveNavitar(id) updates
//   activeNavitarId state in NavitarFightClub, whose persistence
//   effect writes localStorage `glacer-active-navitar-id`;
//   userNavitar is derived from that id, and Battle Step 1,
//   Profile and the Stroll companion all read userNavitar — so a
//   Choose anywhere is the same choice everywhere. No parallel
//   selection state.
//
// Resolution, honestly:
// - You already own a fighter with this name → Choose calls
//   setActiveNavitar(owned.id).
// - Anything else renders nothing — no dead button, no dead
//   check. Locked fighters never render these controls (callers
//   gate on !locked).
//
// OWNED-ONLY (Round 16, Eddie 2026-11-17): "when you go to the
// Navidex you can see the full roster, you would only be able to
// select avatars that you own." The Navidex choose path used to
// ADOPT an unowned showcase fighter on the spot (tap ✓ → it's
// yours and active) — that made every starter ownable by anyone
// from the roster page, which is exactly what Eddie closed.
// Choosing on the Navidex is now owned-only: the ✓ and the Choose
// button render only for fighters already in the player's
// collection, and unowned fighters get the lock treatment
// (ChooseLockButton / LockedChoosePanel below) with the reason.
// Adoption itself is untouched — it lives where it always also
// lived, on the Home page (adopt a starter / create your own,
// with the attacks editor), and a fighter adopted there is owned
// and choosable here immediately. Owner Mode is unchanged: the
// owner's collection IS the full roster (FightClub merges the
// owner records in), so everything is owned and choosable.
import React from 'react';
import { Box, Button, Chip, IconButton, Typography } from '@mui/material';
import CheckIcon from '@mui/icons-material/Check';
import LockIcon from '@mui/icons-material/Lock';
import { useNavitarFightClub } from '../contexts/NavitarFightClub';
import { useNotifications } from '../contexts/NotificationsContext';
import { markSwapReturnPicked } from '../utils/swapReturn';
import { getLockedNavitar } from '../utils/lockedRoster';

// THE one choose path (2026-11-16): every choose control in the
// app — the Stage's "✔ Choose for Battle" button and the ✓ check
// on the Stage card and grid cards — resolves and writes through
// this hook, so there is exactly one selection state underneath
// (FightClub's active navitar / glacer-active-navitar-id).
// Round 16: owned-only (see the header note) — canChoose is
// exactly "this fighter is in the player's collection". In Owner
// Mode the collection includes every design, so the owner's
// checks behave exactly as they always have.
export function useChooseNavitar(name: string, element: string, imageUrl?: string) {
  const { navitars, userNavitar, setActiveNavitar } = useNavitarFightClub();
  const { notify } = useNotifications();

  const owned = navitars.find(n => n.name === name);
  // Round 31 (Eddie): "already chosen" is judged the way the
  // player sees it — the active fighter IS this fighter. The id
  // comparison alone was not enough: resolution here is by NAME,
  // and a collection can hold two records with one name (a created
  // fighter and its roster twin; owner records join the same
  // pool). When the ACTIVE record was the twin, the id check read
  // false while the Stage header already showed the fighter as
  // chosen — so every tap on the gold ✓ "chose" it again and the
  // confirmation popped up over and over. Name equality is the
  // player's truth (the Stage's own chosen state is name-based
  // too), so it counts here.
  const isActive =
    !!owned && !!userNavitar && (userNavitar.id === owned.id || userNavitar.name === name);
  const canChoose = !!owned;

  // Writes glacer-active-navitar-id through FightClub's
  // setActiveNavitar for an owned fighter — and does nothing at
  // all for an unowned one: there is no path from the Navidex
  // that makes an unowned fighter active. Deliberately does NOT
  // navigate. onChosen fires AFTER the write, for presentational
  // celebrations (the Stage's victory flourish) — the choice
  // never depends on it.
  //
  // Round 31 (Eddie): exactly ONE confirmation per actual
  // selection change, delivered as a notification (the R17 store)
  // — "it should pop up as a notification." Choosing the fighter
  // who is already chosen is a complete no-op: no write, no
  // flourish, no pop-up. Switching to a different fighter fires
  // exactly one 'fighter' record; its id is unique per change, so
  // the store's id-dedupe never swallows a genuine switch, and
  // this guard is what stops the repeats.
  const choose = (onChosen?: () => void) => {
    if (!owned) return;
    if (isActive) return;
    setActiveNavitar(owned.id);
    // Round 14: if this pick is a pre-fight swap errand (the
    // player came from Battle Step 1 / the challenge screen via
    // the Navidex swap button), stamp it so the Navidex banner
    // can offer the way back to the pairing. No-op otherwise.
    markSwapReturnPicked(name);
    notify({
      id: `fighter-chosen-${owned.id}-${Date.now()}`,
      kind: 'fighter',
      title: `✔ ${name} is your battle fighter`,
      body: 'Chosen in the Navidex — it fights and strolls for you now.',
      route: '/collection',
      demo: false,
    });
    onChosen?.();
  };

  return { canChoose, isActive, choose, owned: !!owned };
}

// Why this fighter can't be chosen (Round 16): the honest reason,
// in the game's own language. A locked-roster design carries its
// unlock path on its lockedRoster entry (a Prime's season-event
// law, a Deity's "never caught"); Prime Zero is soulbound to
// Eddie; everything else is plain collection state — not owned
// yet, with the real on-ramp named (Home adoption / creation).
// No purchase system is invented here, because there isn't one.
export function lockReasonFor(name: string): string {
  const locked = getLockedNavitar(name);
  if (locked) return locked.unlockLabel;
  if (name === 'Prime Zero')
    return 'Soulbound 1/1 — Eddie’s alone. Never findable, never catchable, never traded.';
  return 'Not in your collection yet — adopt a starter or create your own on the Home page, and it becomes yours to choose.';
}

// The LOCK in the ✓ check's seat (Round 16): same 44px circular
// footprint on the card art / Stage header, but a lock — tapping
// it explains (the caller shows lockReasonFor); it never writes
// selection state. Rendered exactly where ChooseCheckButton
// would have rendered for an owned fighter, so the layout of the
// Navidex does not move — only the fighter's state speaks.
export const ChooseLockButton: React.FC<{
  name: string;
  onTap?: () => void;
}> = ({ name, onTap }) => {
  return (
    <IconButton
      aria-label={`${name} is locked — not in your collection`}
      data-choose-lock={name}
      onClick={e => {
        // A lock tap is an explanation, not a card tap: keep the
        // card art's own tap (its cry) out of this gesture, the
        // same separation the ✓ check keeps.
        e.stopPropagation();
        onTap?.();
      }}
      sx={{
        width: 44,
        height: 44,
        borderRadius: '50%',
        border: '2px solid rgba(255, 213, 79, 0.75)',
        bgcolor: 'rgba(5, 15, 22, 0.66)',
        color: '#ffd54f',
        boxShadow: '0 2px 8px rgba(0,0,0,0.45)',
        backdropFilter: 'blur(2px)',
        '&:hover': { bgcolor: 'rgba(74, 53, 0, 0.55)' },
      }}
    >
      <LockIcon sx={{ fontSize: 22 }} />
    </IconButton>
  );
};

// The locked panel in the Choose button's seat (Round 16): on the
// Navidex Stage, an unowned fighter's "✔ Choose for Battle" slot
// becomes this — a clear lock, the word LOCKED, and the reason —
// in the same place, at the same size, so nothing about the
// Stage's layout shifts between owned and unowned fighters.
export const LockedChoosePanel: React.FC<{ name: string }> = ({ name }) => {
  return (
    <Box
      data-testid="locked-choose-panel"
      data-locked-name={name}
      sx={{
        mt: 1.5,
        p: 1.5,
        borderRadius: 2,
        border: '2px solid rgba(255, 213, 79, 0.55)',
        background: 'rgba(0,0,0,0.35)',
        position: 'relative',
        zIndex: 2,
        textAlign: 'center',
      }}
    >
      <Typography sx={{ fontWeight: 900, color: '#ffd54f', letterSpacing: '0.03em' }}>
        🔒 LOCKED — NOT IN YOUR COLLECTION
      </Typography>
      <Typography variant="body2" sx={{ color: '#cfeef8', mt: 0.5 }}>
        {lockReasonFor(name)}
      </Typography>
    </Box>
  );
};

export const BattleWithButton: React.FC<{
  name: string;
  element: string;
  imageUrl?: string;
  // Optional celebration hook (Navidex Stage, 2026-11-16): fired
  // AFTER the choice is written, so the stage can answer with the
  // fighter's victory flourish. Purely presentational — the
  // choice itself never depends on it.
  onChosen?: () => void;
}> = ({ name, element, imageUrl, onChosen }) => {
  const { canChoose, isActive, choose } = useChooseNavitar(name, element, imageUrl);
  if (!canChoose) return null;

  if (isActive) {
    return (
      <Box
        sx={{
          mt: 1.5,
          p: 1,
          borderRadius: 2,
          border: '2px solid #ffd54f',
          boxShadow: '0 0 0 2px rgba(255,213,79,0.35), 0 0 18px rgba(255,213,79,0.45)',
          background: 'rgba(255,213,79,0.08)',
          position: 'relative',
          zIndex: 2,
        }}
      >
        <Chip
          label="✓ CHOSEN — YOUR BATTLE NAVITAR"
          size="small"
          sx={{ mb: 1, fontWeight: 900, bgcolor: '#ffd54f', color: '#4a3500' }}
        />
        <Button
          variant="contained"
          fullWidth
          disabled
          sx={{
            fontWeight: 900,
            fontSize: '1.05rem',
            py: 1.5,
            '&.Mui-disabled': { bgcolor: '#ffd54f', color: '#4a3500' },
          }}
        >
          ✓ Chosen — Your Battle Navitar
        </Button>
        {/* No "Go to Battle" button (streamlining, 2026-11-16):
            the chosen state IS the confirmation. Getting to Battle
            is the bottom tab bar's job — its Battle tab is always
            one tap away, and Battle Step 1 opens already confirmed
            on this fighter. */}
      </Box>
    );
  }

  return (
    <Box sx={{ mt: 1.5, position: 'relative', zIndex: 2 }}>
      <Button
        variant="contained"
        color="primary"
        size="large"
        fullWidth
        onClick={() => choose(onChosen)}
        aria-label={`Choose ${name} for battle`}
        sx={{ fontWeight: 900, fontSize: '1.1rem', py: 1.75, letterSpacing: '0.02em' }}
      >
        ✔ Choose for Battle
      </Button>
    </Box>
  );
};

// The ✓ CHECK on the card (Eddie, 2026-11-16 ~13:46 PT): a
// circular check sitting on the navitar's card art — on the
// Navidex grid cards and on the Stage's staged-fighter card.
// Tap it and that navitar takes over the role of being with you:
// the SAME write as the Choose button (useChooseNavitar →
// FightClub setActiveNavitar / createUserNavitar →
// glacer-active-navitar-id), the same onChosen celebration hook,
// no navigation, no battle. State reads the same truth: the
// chosen navitar's check is filled gold; every other choosable
// card shows the outlined check. Renders nothing where choosing
// isn't possible (not owned — Round 16 owned-only; the lock
// treatment above takes its place there) and callers never
// render it on locked cards — no dead controls.
export const ChooseCheckButton: React.FC<{
  name: string;
  element: string;
  imageUrl?: string;
  onChosen?: () => void;
}> = ({ name, element, imageUrl, onChosen }) => {
  const { canChoose, isActive, choose } = useChooseNavitar(name, element, imageUrl);
  if (!canChoose) return null;

  return (
    <IconButton
      aria-label={isActive ? `${name} is your chosen navitar` : `Choose ${name} as your navitar`}
      aria-pressed={isActive}
      data-choose-check={name}
      data-chosen={isActive ? 'true' : undefined}
      onClick={e => {
        // The check is a pick, not a card tap: keep the card
        // art's own tap (its cry) out of this gesture.
        e.stopPropagation();
        if (!isActive) choose(onChosen);
      }}
      sx={{
        // ≥40px hit area (44px) around a 36px visual circle.
        width: 44,
        height: 44,
        borderRadius: '50%',
        border: isActive ? '2px solid #ffd54f' : '2px solid rgba(234, 246, 250, 0.85)',
        bgcolor: isActive ? '#ffd54f' : 'rgba(5, 15, 22, 0.5)',
        color: isActive ? '#4a3500' : '#eaf6fa',
        boxShadow: isActive
          ? '0 0 16px rgba(255, 213, 79, 0.85), 0 2px 8px rgba(0,0,0,0.45)'
          : '0 2px 8px rgba(0,0,0,0.45)',
        backdropFilter: 'blur(2px)',
        transition: 'background-color 0.25s ease, box-shadow 0.25s ease, border-color 0.25s ease',
        '&:hover': {
          bgcolor: isActive ? '#ffd54f' : 'rgba(18, 165, 199, 0.35)',
        },
      }}
    >
      <CheckIcon sx={{ fontSize: 25, fontWeight: 900 }} />
    </IconButton>
  );
};

export default BattleWithButton;
